/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  Catalyst pellet: a 3 mm spherical gamma-alumina support.

  *** THIS IS A TEACHING SURROGATE.  NO NUMBER IN IT IS CITED. ***

  And that sentence is not only in this banner: `provenance.identity.origin` is
  read by the engine and ANNOUNCED on every run that uses this record, because
  a field the engine cannot see is a comment.

  It is declared HERE, case-locally, and NOT in data/standards/assets/, and
  that placement is the honest half of the statement.  data/standards/ is the
  frozen, committee-managed tree in which every value is expected to carry a
  PRIMARY citation; the two numbers that matter most to the answer this case
  computes -- the intraparticle porosity `epsilon_p` and the tortuosity `tau`
  -- are exactly the two this author could not source from a primary.  Rather
  than attach a citation that does not support them (which converts *unsourced*
  into *falsely sourced*, and neither a reader nor a gate can detect that), the
  values are stated as what they are: round, plausible, uncited, and chosen so
  the resulting Thiele modulus lands in the transition region where the
  concentration field is worth looking at.

  WHAT IS VERIFIED IN THIS CASE, and it is not these numbers: that the
  NUMERICAL solution of the intraparticle boundary-value problem reproduces the
  first-order isothermal CLOSED FORM.  That claim is independent of every value
  below -- change the porosity and the modulus moves, and the numerical field
  still has to match the analytical field at the new modulus.  See the README.

  Promoting a real, cited catalyst into data/standards/assets/ needs no code
  change: `CatalystRegistry` already scans that home for `kind catalyst;`.
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

kind catalyst;

catalyst
{
    name         aluminaSphere3mm;
    type         "gamma-alumina support, spherical pellet (teaching surrogate)";

    geometry     sphere;
    radius       1.5 mm;         // 3 mm pellet

    rho_particle 1300;           // kg/m3, apparent (pellet) density
    rho_bulk      780;           // kg/m3, packed bulk density

    epsilon_p    0.45;           // intraparticle porosity [-]
    tau          3.0;            // tortuosity [-]
}

reviewStatus  interim;

provenance
{
    identity
    {
        origin teachingSurrogate;
        method "Round values in the range commonly quoted for a porous gamma-alumina support pellet.  NOT taken from, and NOT traceable to, any primary measurement.  epsilon_p and tau together set D_eff = (epsilon_p/tau)*D_molecular, and tau alone is conventionally reported anywhere between 2 and 7 -- so a factor of three in eta sits inside the uncertainty of this record.  Do not quote it.";
    }
}
